A turn that ends costs its thread nothing.
A thread running all along would never spend its units, and keep its requests due as early as a thread that waited;
every count of a turn on units moves its payer's virtual time on TIME_UNITS / units counts.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a step of the clock did not charge the thread whose turn it was its units' part
Report: a traced call that moved no time charged the thread whose turn it was
Witness: fuzz bind-turn-later

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -496,9 +496,9 @@ static uint64_t turn_charge(struct core *core)
 {
     uint64_t now = timer_now();
     struct place *p = turn_place(core);
     if (p != NULL) {
-        p->vt = turn_vtime(core, p, now);
+        p->vt = turn_vtime(core, p, core->turn_from);
     }
     core->turn_from = now;
     return now;
 }
